// SHIFT TABLES - a shift moves through three tables that share one layout (craa5_name, craa5_boardjson, craa5_updatesjson, ...):
//   craa5_shiftplan    a setup for a future shift. Only ever loaded for its own crew and exact shift start, and only when someone presses
//                      Load Plan; once saved as the live board it is marked used and deactivated.
//   craa5_shiftboard   the shift on now: Save Progress writes the whole board into this one row (one write, no reads). Shift Start and
//                      Ganttly read its rows straight out of the JSON (they look exactly like the old craa5_taskassignment rows).
//   craa5_shiftarchive the shift once it is over: written at Shift Handoff, or by whoever opens Shift Start or Ganttly once the shift
//                      ended more than 4 hours ago (they are told). The live row is then deactivated, so the live table stays tiny.
// craa5_shiftlog keeps who opened which board and every change saved. craa5_taskassignment is only read: its old rows are imported into
// the archive from the console and, once checked, retired (deactivated, never deleted).
// ============================================================================
